# Sovereign: every path requires founder review before merge.
# Ruleset 25374786 on `main` requires one approval and Code Owner review (verified 2026-10-27).
# GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from the PR's target branch, so this file is enforced only once it exists
# there: until it is on `main`, any approval from an account with write access satisfies the rule.
# Coding agents open PRs as `owlbuilder`, because GitHub does not let an author approve their own PR
# (docs/engineering/GITHUB-GOVERNANCE-SETUP.md, decision D-F).
# The last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all stays first (tests/test_policy_invariants.py).
# The explicit entries below mark the kernel, governance and automation paths (Tier 2 in
# docs/DEVELOPMENT.md); the catch-all alone does not make a change Tier 2.

